  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Occasionally I find myself wanting to enter an animation using a parameter not directly related to a toggle. I.E. an animator that uses an integer to enter multiple toggle animations that are driven by a parameter driver, on a single layer, I'd like it to show the user the toggled parameter instead of the parameter the animation is entering on. A direct blendtree *would* work in this scenario, but I do not like the mixed WD required.\n\nI think this would be much more relevant for buttons entering the animation, so perhaps the option to visually see which state a parameter is in using a button.\n\nThis would absolutely only be for more advanced animators, but hiding it behind an option should solve any confusion.",
